  "contentHtml": "\n\n                    <!-- Display video article in news article for the custom next story -->\n                    \n                    <!-- Modifying the body placing embeds,promoslots,related etc.-->\n                                        <figure><img src=\"/images/default.jpg\" alt=\"\"></figure><p>New Delhi: Australia-based global safety solutions company <a href=\"/tag/ansell+limited\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ansell Limited</a> plans to invest $60 million in India as it sets up a new manufacturing facility for <a href=\"/tag/surgical+gloves\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">surgical gloves</a>.The company said the proposed facility is expected to cater to the growing demand for high-quality surgical gloves in India and international markets, while further strengthening Ansell’s supply chain and manufacturing footprint.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>Ansell added that this reflects its confidence in the Indian healthcare and <a href=\"/tag/medical+devices\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">medical devices</a> sector which has witnessed increasing demand for medical consumables and protective products, driven by the expansion of healthcare infrastructure, rising awareness around infection prevention and the need for high-quality medical product.</p>\n                            <p>Advt\n                            </p>\n\n                              \n                                                         \n                        <p>\"The investment is primarily to cater to the domestic market and to export to the US and Europe,\" said Nathalie Ahlström, MD &amp; CEO, Ansell of the company.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>Details of the location of the proposed facility remain unclear at the time of publication.                    </p><!-- Category Most Read Placement -->\n                                                                    \n                                                        